### MVP LOOP STATE (END OF SESSION 13)

The complete v0.1 MVP dictation loop works end-to-end:

1. popo boots → tray icon in notification area, pill at bottom-center,
   main window hidden.
2. User clicks into any text field.
3. User holds Ctrl+Shift+Space.
4. Rust captures `GetForegroundWindow()` HWND + current clipboard.
5. cpal opens default mic (48 kHz typically, f32/i16/u16 handled).
6. Pill morphs sleep → ready → active.
7. Tokio task pumps 16-bar RMS waveform events at 25 Hz → pill bars
   animate with user's voice.
8. User releases.
9. cpal stream drops (audio stops), waveform task stops.
10. Pill morphs to processing (DotMatrix loader).
11. `gcp::fake_transcribe` returns a canned string after 800 ms.
    **This is the one remaining fake piece — swap to real Chirp gRPC
    in Phase 2 [6] polish.**
12. Paste orchestrator runs:
    arboard.set_text(transcript) → SetForegroundWindow(captured HWND)
    → 50 ms dwell → enigo Ctrl+V → 100 ms dwell → verify foreground
    unchanged → arboard.set_text(prev_clipboard) restore.
13. Transcript appears at the user's cursor in the target app.
14. Pill flashes success (Check icon, 300 ms).
15. Pill morphs back to sleep.

What's needed to ship v0.1 beyond this:
- **Phase 2 [6] polish**: swap `fake_transcribe` for real Chirp gRPC.
  This is the biggest remaining piece. Needs proto vendoring +
  tonic-build + protoc on PATH + gcp_auth token caching.
- **Phase 3 [9]**: end-to-end validation across the paste test matrix
  (docs/PASTE_MECHANICS.md §9). Already working for Chrome / VS Code
  / Slack / Notepad / most apps thanks to enigo primary; need to run
  the full grid.
- **Phase 4 polish bundle**: History filter chips (modesStore is
  ready), Modes set-as-default UI, confirm-before-delete, Firebase
  sign-in.
- **Phase 5 [16]+[17]**: paste test suite across all app categories,
  README setup guide.

